<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  MLIE_FAUNA_ABSORPTION_1 Wave B — BodyDefs for the 3 species this wave ports that
  need a non-vanilla body (Dewback, Acklay, Wampa). Vulptex, Porg and Nuna use
  vanilla Core bodies (QuadrupedAnimalWithPawsAndTail / Bird) and need none.

  Ported verbatim from mlie.starwarsanimalcollection's Bodies/Bodies_Animal_StarWars.xml,
  one BodyDef per species, renamed RSW_<Species> to match the ThingDef's own
  <race><body> reference in RSW_Dewback.xml / RSW_Acklay.xml / RSW_Wampa.xml.
  Geometry (part coverage, groups, custom labels) is unchanged; only the defName and
  the custom body-part-group references (RSW_SWTailAttackTool,
  RSW_SWLeftLegClawAttackTool, RSW_SWRightLegClawAttackTool, RSW_SWLeftFingerClaw,
  RSW_SWRightFingerClaw — see RSW_MlieWaveB_BodyParts.xml) and the custom
  BodyPartDef (RSW_SW_Club, RSW_SW_LeftClaw — same file) were repointed. Every other
  <def> referenced (Body, Tail, Spine, Shell, Elytra, InsectHeart, Pronotum,
  InsectHead, InsectLeg, Skull, Brain, Eye, Nose, AnimalJaw, Antenna, InsectNostril,
  InsectMouth, Foot, Neck, Leg, Paw, Arm, Hand, Finger, Torso, Waist, Shoulder,
  Clavicle, Humerus, Radius, Ribcage, Sternum, Pelvis, Femur, Tibia, Toe, Ear,
  Kidney, Liver, Lung, Heart, Stomach) is vanilla Core/Anomaly — confirmed via
  RimSage, no donor BodyDef dependency beyond this file's own RSW_ parts.

  Acklay is themed as an armored arthropod (leatherDef RSW_Leather_Crustapod,
  specificMeatDef RSW_Crustapod_Meat) — the InsectLeg/InsectHead/Elytra/Pronotum
  parts are the donor's own choice, not a porting error.
-->
